After my recent 1st ascension as valkyrie, I decided to try playing
samurai. I started very carefully, but still I couldn't get far and got
4-5 samurais killed very soon. Then RGN smiled at me.

This time I took more chances right from the start, and it payed off. I
was in some sort of trouble -- can't remember exactly what -- but that
lead to reading un-id'd scrolls and trying on un-id'd rings and amu.
One of the rings was ring of conflict, and amu at least didn't do
anything bad so I left it on. Scrolls were not bad either, a couple of
enchant weapon scrolls so my katana was +3.

Went to Sokoban 1st, got BoH. After getting this far in one piece I
decided to cut down risks and move on more cautiously.

Second level in Mines had bones. There seemed to be 2 or 3 piles (is
that possible - or were there only one which creatures had scattered?).
SDSM, Excalibur, 3 magic markers, tinning kit and another BoH.
Thank-you-very-much, "Monkly Business 18, killed by a mumak". Well,
SDSM and Excalibur were in another pile, and they were not cursed,
which is something that puzzled me (and do still).

My luck continued, and minetown had co-aligned altar. From mines I also
found magic whistle, which was very much needed since from the bag/sack
I found from the bones pile two soldier ants hatched, mistake me for
daddy and become my pets. So I had 2 soldier ants and 2 two dogs.
Great, now I only needed poly trap (never found one).

As RGN made everything easy for me, I did everything I possibly could
to spoil it. I nearly got killed by a troll. I just couldn't kill it no
matter how many times I hit it. My HP went down, so I escaped with wand
of diggin, and the troll dropped after me! I had plenty of potions, but
I hadn't id'd healing potions. My HP went to 5, but praying restored my
health. Then I noticed a message saying that I'm whacking monsters with
a tin opener, slapped myself on the forehead and switched to Excalibur.
Troll died with a couple of hits, but still kept being annoying and
didn't stay dead long enought to get tinned. Eventually it did.

Soon after this I was tinning some giants, which took my attention and
I failed to notice a pyrolisk. Apparently my SDSM didn't reflect its
gaze, as it it killed me, but then amulet turned out to be "of life
saving!

After long search I found *cross*-aligned unicorn, so I could start
identifying all the potions I had collected so far. One was potion of
polymorph, and my unicorn horn turned to a crystal ball (this left me
clueless, and had to come here for help).

On my way back up to minetown to donate for protection, I noticed a
store that I had missed earlier. There was a Frost Brand. Nice. My dog
stole loads of crap from that store but just didn't touch the sword
(could it be generated as cursed?). Oh well, I'm going to get it on my
way down again, I thought.

Back in minetown I donated all my money and got some protection. Then I
thought I'm going to get crowned while I'm there. /oM created a yeti,
which turned to flee. I chased it, killed it and started carrying it
back to the altar. It was heavy and I became overtaxed. Then an energy
vortex showed up. Big deal, I thought. It engulfed me. I couldn't fight
while overtaxed. It spit me out, but engulfed me so soon that I didn't
have time to drop the yeti. This happened over and over again. I was
getting weak. I don't know why I didn't think of the obvious before,
but when I did it was too late; I tried dropping yeti while being
engufled, and (of course) it worked! But I only got to swing my sword
once. DYWYPI?

I could have prayed, I could have drank potion of healing. I could have
dropped yeti immediately after being engulfed. This was the most stupid
death I've suffered in Nethack.



